Portions of the ToneBoosters/UAPP normalization and XML mapping are based on
SiliconExarch/EqConverter, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Source: https://github.com/SiliconExarch/EqConverter
License: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The implementation in this repository is a native Kotlin/Android port of the
established weekssa/opra-uapp-converter conversion behavior and has been
substantially rewritten for validated multi-source catalog ingestion, OPRA
compatibility/base ingestion, provenance and revision handling, Room-managed
local user state, background reconciliation, Android Storage Access Framework
export/recovery, supported local USB-DAC management, and native app UX.

Third-party EQ data remains subject to source-specific rights and attribution.
OPRA-derived headphone and EQ data is separately licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
The runtime canonical catalog may also contain qualified structured EQ records
from sources with other terms, including specifically qualified MIT-licensed
creator/repository and General-EQ sources, plus provenance-preserving qualified
community records under the maintained source policy.

EQ Library does not treat the application Apache-2.0 license as a blanket
license for third-party EQ data, source prose, images, or measurements.
See DATA_LICENSE.md, config/source_registry.json, and
`docs/SOURCE_INGESTION_STRATEGY.md` for data attribution, publication boundaries,
and source-specific policy details.
